- **Graham:** he wrote nearly all the core parsing code, and he has committed 8 times in the last 90 days. Priscila wrote only `Comments.php` and `Interpolator.php`, and she committed 2 times in the same period.
- **Bus factor:** it is 1 for the core of `src/Parser/`. If Graham left, most of the module would have no author who knows the current code. Priscila is the only other person with real ownership, and only of the two newest files.
- **Not reviewers:** Vance Lucas, Jonas Staudenmeir and JT Smith have 1.3% of the lines combined. Marta Kowalczyk has a recent commit but no surviving lines at this path, so I'd leave them out.
- **Limits:**
  - I did not run the skill's dependents count for importance, because you only asked about reviewers.
  - `git blame` shows who wrote a line, not who understands it today. Treat Priscila as the review backup for the core files, not as an equal owner.

I did not run the skill's default commit-count workflow, and I did not use its contributor-analyzer agent.

